<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Kamau estimated the lower quartile, <m>Q_{ {1} }</m>, of the masses, in kg (to the nearest kg), of <m>{77}</m> goats sold at Kiunga market. His working has one mistake.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Mass (kg)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m>–<m>{19}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20}</m>–<m>{29}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{30}</m>–<m>{39}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{40}</m>–<m>{49}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{50}</m>–<m>{59}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{60}</m>–<m>{69}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Frequency (<m>f</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{7}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{16}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{14}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{13}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{7}</m></cell></row></tabular><ol><li><m>n = {77}</m></li><li>Position of <m>Q_{ {1} }</m>: <m>{77} \div 4</m> <m>= {19.25}</m></li><li>The cumulative frequencies are 7, 23, 43, 57, 70, 77, so <m>Q_{ {1} }</m> is in the class <m>{20}</m>–<m>{29}</m>.</li><li><m>L = {20}</m></li><li><m>CF = {7}</m>, <m>F = {16}</m>, <m>c = 10</m></li><li><m>Q_{ {1} } = {20} + \dfrac{ {19.25} - {7} }{ {16} } \times 10 \approx {27.7}</m> kg</li></ol><p>(a) Which step has the mistake?</p><div>[ Step 1 | Step 2 | Step 3 | Step 4 | Step 5 | Step 6 ]  </div><p>(b) Give the correct value of <m>Q_{ {1} }</m>, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><div><m>Q_{ {1} } =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/> kg  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Check each value that goes into the formula <m>Q_{ {1} } = L + \dfrac{\text{position} - CF}{F} \times c</m>: for grouped data the position is <m>n/4</m> or <m>3n/4</m> with no <m>+1</m>; <m>L</m> is the lower class boundary, because the masses are to the nearest kg; and <m>CF</m> is the cumulative frequency of the class before the quartile class.</p><p>(a) The mistake is in Step 4. <m>{20}</m> is the lower class limit. The class <m>{20}</m>–<m>{29}</m> starts at the lower class boundary, <m>{19.5}</m>.</p><p>(b) <me>Q_{ {1} } = {19.5} + \frac{ {19.25} - {7} }{ {16} } \times 10 \approx {27.2}\text{ kg}</me></p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>Step 4</p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{869}{32}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>